// The browser run, which the tsconfig above deliberately does not describe.
//
// A second program rather than one more entry in that file's `include`, and the
// reason is `types: []`: nothing in src/ may see an ambient Node global, because
// that bundle runs in a browser where `process` is a ReferenceError only
// production finds. env.d.ts beside this declares the one global the spec reads,
// and adding e2e/ to the app's program would hand that declaration to src/ too.
//
// Here rather than ../tsconfig.e2e.json so that typescript-eslint's project
// service finds it: it resolves the nearest tsconfig.json walking up from each
// file, which is also what gives the spec its type-aware rules — no-floating-
// promises most of all, since a missing await on an expect is a Playwright
// assertion that silently passes.
//
// Everything else is inherited, so the strictness the bundle is held to is the
// strictness the spec is held to, which is the point of covering it at all.
{
  "extends": "../tsconfig.json",
  "include": ["."]
}
